version 2.0

* modernized the package using Rcpp and ggplot2 
* Package was profiles and repetitive overhead eliminated
* comprehensive test suite written
* logistic regression estimation and weibull survival estimation were coded in C++ using RcppEigen for vast speedups
* Parallelization improved using mirai (for windows) and forking (for *nix)
* Compile flags optimize for user's specific hardware
* fixed a bug in the difference_function branch
* fixed rendering issues in the documentation

version 1.7

* Calculated and prints basic and studentized bootstrap confidence intervals by default
* Fixed warnings

version 1.6

* Decomped plot parameter into a separate function for ease of use
* Removed num_cores parameter. Please use the more standard options(mc.cores = ...)
* Corrected paper examples (on github page)

version 1.5

* Support for survival endpoints 
* Support for incidence endpoints: odds ratio, risk ratio and probability difference
* Better arguments / defaults for the main function "PTE_bootstrap_inference"
* Customization for non-standard metrics for all endpoints
* Speed improvements
* Better documentation

version 1.0

* Initial Release